hadiths[18]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19689","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Asim ibn Urwah ibn Masud al-Thaqafi narrated to me, that Amr ibn al-Sharid narrated to him that his father narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man drinks, then flog him. Then if he drinks, then flog him, four times or five times. Then if he drinks, then kill him."
"19690","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim informed us from Amr ibn Shuayb, Amr ibn al-Sharid narrated to me from his father al-Sharid ibn Suwayd, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, land in which no one has partnership nor division except neighbourhood. He said: The neighbour is more entitled to his adjoining property as long as it is."
"19691","Rawh narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, and al-Khaffaf informed us, Husayn, from Amr ibn Shuayb from Amr ibn al-Sharid from his father al-Sharid ibn Suwayd, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah— al-Khaffaf said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, land in which no one has partnership nor division except neighbourhood. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbour is more entitled to his adjoining property as long as it is."
"19692","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Wabr ibn Abi Dulaylah informed me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Maymun ibn Musaykah informed me, he said: Amr ibn al-Sharid narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay by one who can pay makes lawful his honour and his punishment."
"19693","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala ibn Kab al-Taifi narrated to us from Amr ibn al-Sharid from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him to recite from the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt. He said: I recited to him a hundred rhymes, and I did not recite anything to him but he said: More, more, until when I finished a hundred rhymes he said: He almost accepted Islam."
"19694","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maysarah informed us that he heard Yaqub ibn Asim ibn Urwah saying: I heard al-Sharid saying: I bear witness, I stood with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafat. He said: His two feet did not touch the ground until he came to Jam."
"19695","Muhanna ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: My father, his kunyah Abu Shibl, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from al-Sharid, that his mother bequeathed that a believing slave be freed on her behalf. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother bequeathed that a believing slave be freed on her behalf, and with me is a black Nubian slave-girl. He said: Call her. He brought her, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Who is your Lord. She said: Allah. He said: Who am I. She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Free her, for she is a believer."
"19696","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maysarah narrated to us that he heard Amr ibn al-Sharid saying: Al-Sharid said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: Do you have with you any of the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt. I said: Yes. He said: Recite to me. I recited to him a verse, and he kept saying to me whenever I recited a verse to him: More, until I recited to him a hundred verses. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent and I fell silent."
"19697","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Amr ibn al-Sharid from his father, he said: A leprous man of Thaqif came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Go to him and inform him that I have pledged to him, so let him return."
"19698","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abdullah Abu Yala al-Taifi narrated to us from Amr ibn al-Sharid from his father, and Abu Amir said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn al-Sharid narrating from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbour is more entitled to his adjoining property than another. Abu Amir said in his hadith: A person is more entitled."
"19699","Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad Abu Ubaydah narrated to us from Khalaf, meaning Ibn Mihran, Amir al-Ahwal narrated to us from Salih ibn Dinar from Amr ibn al-Sharid, he said: I heard al-Sharid saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever kills a sparrow in vain, it will cry out to Allah Mighty and Majestic on the Day of Resurrection because of him, saying: O Lord, so-and-so killed me in vain and did not kill me for benefit."
"19700","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maysarah informed us that he heard Yaqub ibn Asim ibn Urwah saying: I heard al-Sharid, he said: I bear witness, I poured forth with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his two feet did not touch the ground until he came to Jam. And once he said: I stood with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafat, and it did not touch. My father said: Where Rawh said: I stood with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he dictated it from his book."
"19701","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, haddathana Ibrahim ibn Maysarah that he heard Amr ibn al-Sharid narrating from his father: that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, followed a man from Thaqif until he hurried after him until he seized his garment and said: Raise your izar. He said: So the man uncovered his knees and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am bow-legged and my knees knock together. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: All the creation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, is good. He said: And that man was not seen thereafter except with his izar to the middle of his shins until he died."
"19702","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Zakariyya, haddathana Ibrahim ibn Maysarah that he heard Amr ibn al-Sharid saying: It reached us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man who was lying asleep on his face, and he said: This is the most hateful manner of lying to Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He."
"19703","Haddathana Hushaym ibn Bashir, from Yala ibn Ata, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father, he said: There was in the delegation of Thaqif a leprous man, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to him: Go back, for I have pledged allegiance with you."
"19704","Haddathana Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father, or from Yaqub ibn Asim, that he heard al-Sharid saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man dragging his izar, so he hastened to him, or hurried, and said: Raise your izar and fear Allah. He said: I am bow-legged, my knees knock together. So he said: Raise your izar, for all the creation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, is good. So that man was not seen afterwards except with his izar reaching the middle of his shins, or to the middle of his shins."
"19705","Haddathana Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father, if Allah wills, or Yaqub ibn Asim, meaning from al-Sharid, thus our father narrated it to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mounted me behind him and said: Do you have any of the poetry of Umayyah with you. I said: Yes. He said: Recite to me. So I recited to him a verse, and he said: More. He kept saying: More, until I had recited to him one hundred verses."
"19706","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said, from Husayn al-Muallim, haddathana Amr ibn Shuayb, haddathani Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father al-Sharid ibn Suwayd, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, land in which no one has a partner or a share except for neighborhood. He said: The neighbor has more right to his adjoining property, as long as it is."
